{
  "kanji": "並",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 並\ntitle: line up; parallel\njlpt: 2\ntags: [jlpt-n2, grade-6, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 8\nradical: 一\nradicalNumber: 1\nonyomi: [ヘイ, ホウ]\nkunyomi: [な.み, なみ, なら.べる, なら.ぶ, なら.びに]\ndistractors: [立, 業, 半]\n---\n\n# 並 — line up; parallel\n\n**Strokes:** 8 · **Key (radical):** 一 (no. 1) · **JLPT:** N2 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n並 brings things into a line or puts them on a comparable level. 並ぶ ならぶ describes things lining up; 並べる ならべる describes arranging them. 並み なみ can instead mean an ordinary level or being on a par with something.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** Imagine two upright objects standing side by side on the same long base line.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ヘイ | on | 並列 へいれつ - arrangement in parallel; parallel connection |\n| ホウ | on | Source-only reading; see the qualification below. |\n| な.み | kun | 並み なみ - average; medium |\n| なみ | kun | 並 なみ - average; medium; [並木](../words/並木.md) なみき - roadside trees; row of trees |\n| なら.べる | kun | [並べる](../words/並べる.md) ならべる - to line up; to set up |\n| なら.ぶ | kun | [並ぶ](../words/並ぶ.md) ならぶ - to line up; to stand in a line |\n| なら.びに | kun | 並びに ならびに - and (also); both ... and |\n\nKANJIDIC2 also records `ホウ`. No matching word example was established in the inspected JMdict snapshot. These are character-dictionary readings for lookup, not recommendations to use this kanji as an everyday spelling of a word.\n\n## Common words\n\n- [並行](../words/並行.md) へいこう - proceeding side by side; concurrency\n- [並ぶ](../words/並ぶ.md) ならぶ - line up; stand in a row\n- [並べる](../words/並べる.md) ならべる - arrange in a row\n- 並み なみ - average; ordinary level\n- [並木](../words/並木.md) なみき - roadside trees; row of trees\n\n## Notes\n\n- 並ぶ is intransitive; 並べる is transitive. 人が並ぶ ひとがならぶ means people line up; 椅子を並べる いすをならべる means arrange chairs.\n- 並びに ならびに is a formal connector meaning 'and' or 'as well as', rather than an instruction to arrange something.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-10-21 snapshot. Word pairs: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1508350, 1508380, 1508390, 1508480, 1508530, 1599620, 1599640.\n",
